invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: sha512.c picks the copy's compression function on a macro no build
  defines, so sha512_hw.c's copy for x86-64 compresses on
  sha512_compress_blocks.c, the plain C the calls without _hw run. A
  session with CH_CPU_AVX2 then runs no kernel. sha512_avx2.c still
  compiles and links and defines a function nobody calls, and every
  digest, every equivalence case and every published vector passes,
  because the plain C computes the same bytes; only the time is wrong, by
  the factor docs/decisions.md 128 measures. The design refuses a silent
  fall back: a host object is a statement about what the object contains.
  The script compiles sha512_hw.c for x86-64 with the pinned clang and
  requires its object to call sha512_avx2_compress_blocks and not
  sha512_compress_blocks, on every machine.

--- old
#ifdef CH_SHA512_AVX2_COPY
#include "sha512_avx2.h"
--- new
#ifdef CH_SHA512_AVX2_KERNEL
#include "sha512_avx2.h"
